>         rdfs:comment "BattGPT extension axiom on the imported BatteryCell class: requires at least one emmo:hasRole value of type battgpt:BatteryRole. Reuses EMMO's own Role/Whole/hasRole mechanism (hasRole domain=Whole, range=Role; BatteryRole is already subClassOf Role) rather than inventing a new property — no new property was created for this. BatteryCell's own EMMO definition already describes it as 'an assembly of electrodes, electrolyte, container, terminals and usually separators', i.e. a Whole whose defining parts include role-players; this axiom formalizes that. Because hasRole's domain is emmo:Whole, this restriction entails BatteryCell is a Whole via domain propagation, so no separate subClassOf Whole assertion is needed. Establishes the path BatteryCell -hasRole-> BatteryRole -usesMaterial-> ChemicalSubstance, which was previously unconnected. Verified in a disposable test copy under both ROBOT+ELK and ROBOT+HermiT (full merged closure): introduces zero new unsatisfiable classes; the ontology still shows only the same two pre-existing, EMMO-internal unsatisfiable classes (CentiMetreSecondDegreeCelsius, MagneticMoment) that exist with or without this axiom. Three further role-specific existence restrictions added in this pass (semantic_enrichment_audit.md Phase 8, validated in battgpt_candidate.ttl): every functioning cell modeled in this KG's scope has a positive electrode, a negative electrode, and an electrolyte role filled (blended/composite electrodes and multi-component electrolytes mean these are 'some', never exactly-1). A SeparatorRole restriction was deliberately NOT added: all-solid-state cells can be separator-free, and this class's own comment already hedges 'usually separators', not 'always' — the open-world test fails for that one, so it stays unconstrained."@en .
